---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Is GEO replacing SEO?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "No: they coexist. Search still drives the majority of traffic, but AI answers are a growing discovery channel. The signals overlap significantly."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How do I get cited by ChatGPT?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Allow OAI-SearchBot (distinct from GPTBot), publish clear factual content, use structured data, and maintain domain trust signals (DNSSEC, authentication)."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Does GEO require different content?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Not fundamentally: clear, well-structured, factual content serves both. The additions are machine-readability (schema, llms.txt) and deliberate crawler policy."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Can I measure AI citations?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Manually: query AI engines with relevant questions and note citations. Automated tools are emerging but immature."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Is GEO relevant for small sites?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Yes, arguably more so: AI engines evaluate content quality rather than domain authority alone, giving smaller sites a citation opportunity."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How is GEO related to AI readiness?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "AI readiness is the technical foundation (DNS, DNSSEC, crawler access, llms.txt). GEO is the content strategy built on that foundation."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Generative Engine Optimization (GEO): The Complete Guide"
  description="generative engine optimization GEO"
  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/ai-web-infrastructure/" class="hover:text-accent">AI Web Infrastructure</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Generative Engine Optimization (GEO): The Complete Guide</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">Generative Engine Optimization (GEO): The Complete Guide</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">GEO is the practice of optimizing your content to be cited by AI answer engines (ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini) rather than ranked by traditional search. The signals overlap with SEO but add machine-readability.</p>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">How GEO differs from SEO</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60"><table class="pdns-table"><tbody><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Goal</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Rank in a list of links</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Be cited as a source in an AI answer</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Optimization target</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Keywords, backlinks, page speed</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Machine-readability, structured data, authority signals</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Discovery path</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">User clicks a link</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">AI quotes your content with a citation</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Measurement</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Rankings, organic traffic</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Citation frequency, brand mentions in AI answers</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">The GEO checklist</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li><strong class="text-ink">Allow AI crawlers</strong> in robots.txt (deliberately, not by accident). <a href="/ai-crawler-checker/">Check your verdicts</a>.</li><li><strong class="text-ink">Publish llms.txt</strong> to give models a curated map. <a href="/llms-txt-generator/">Generate one</a>.</li><li><strong class="text-ink">Enable DNSSEC</strong> and full email authentication: domain-level trust signals. <a href="/what-is-dnssec/">Enable it</a>.</li><li><strong class="text-ink">Add structured data</strong> so entities are unambiguous. <a href="/schema-validator/">Validate your schema</a>.</li><li><strong class="text-ink">Create citable content</strong>: clear definitions, step-by-step processes, unique data. Content that answers a question completely gets cited.</li></ol>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Measuring GEO</h2>
      <p>Ask ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Gemini questions your target audience would ask, and note whether your domain is cited. Track this monthly: AI citation is binary (cited or not), making it easier to measure than traditional rankings.</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is GEO replacing SEO?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No: they coexist. Search still drives the majority of traffic, but AI answers are a growing discovery channel. The signals overlap significantly.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I get cited by ChatGPT?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Allow OAI-SearchBot (distinct from GPTBot), publish clear factual content, use structured data, and maintain domain trust signals (DNSSEC, authentication).</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does GEO require different content?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Not fundamentally: clear, well-structured, factual content serves both. The additions are machine-readability (schema, llms.txt) and deliberate crawler policy.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I measure AI citations?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Manually: query AI engines with relevant questions and note citations. Automated tools are emerging but immature.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is GEO relevant for small sites?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes, arguably more so: AI engines evaluate content quality rather than domain authority alone, giving smaller sites a citation opportunity.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How is GEO related to AI readiness?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">AI readiness is the technical foundation (DNS, DNSSEC, crawler access, llms.txt). GEO is the content strategy built on that foundation.</p></details></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Related</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2"><li><a href="/ai-readiness-guide/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">AI readiness guide →</a></li><li><a href="/ai-crawlers-list/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">AI crawlers list →</a></li><li><a href="/what-is-llms-txt/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">What is llms.txt →</a></li></ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
